Subject: [PATCH 1/3] =?UTF-8?q?fix(sim):=20a=20tilted=20band's=20column=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?dips=20by=20the=20rim's=20exact=20R=C2=B7sin=20=CE=B8?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The leaning column of the reach laws stood each band's bottom one whole
radius under its foot. Just above the upright tolerance of #938 an r 12
holder 5 mm clear of a part read 12 mm lower and was convicted
ShankHit { part: true }: a cliff at 1e-9 rad that any commanded tilt
paid.

One helper, verify::tilt_band::lean, now builds the column for every
law that reads a leaning stack - reach (c), its mid-turn sweep (c3), the
fixture band column (c2) and the tilted rapid (d2). The centre and
radius are the sums they were; the z planes stand at the band's true
lowest and highest points, foot -/+ R·sin θ (a unit vector square to the
axis has a z part of at most sin θ, reached at the rim). An axis off
unit length reads the larger sine, a zero or non-finite one the whole
radius: never shallower than the band. Upright branches are untouched.

Verdicts that move: tilted moves only, toward clean only, where the old
extra depth was what met the material. tilt_tolerance.rs (#938) no
longer expects a holder 5 mm over the stock to convict at 1.01e-9 rad;
it pins the conviction at 20 degrees, where the rim is in the stock.
No golden or posted output changes.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/tilt_band_dip.rs (clean at small tilts, a
rim in the part convicts from 0.6 to 60 degrees, monotone across the
tolerance, the mid-turn sweep) and the tilt_band unit tests (4000-case
containment property, limits, the (c2) column). The posed capsule
sweep's end caps keep the same cliff in the fixture verdict: #1305.

Fixes #1303

