From 3cee560caa6308dfafd83beec296a5c782f14926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:43:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(sim): (c3) reads a span's own floor where its lerp
 can lean past the samples
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The exact rim dip in the mid-turn sweep assumed an in-between pose is
never more tilted than its more tilted sample. That holds only while
every A and B letter of both samples stays inside (-90, 90) degrees
(cos θ = cos A·cos B, -ln cos convex there); past it the lerp can lean
further than both samples (A 100 -> 260 passes straight down; A = B
60 -> 120 holds 75.5 degrees at both ends and 90 between). The old
whole radius did not cover that either: the axial part moves too.

verify::tilt_span::span_floor bounds such a span from the interval of
cos θ the lerp can reach; each pose sample reads the lower of its own
exact bottom and the floors of the spans it ends. Inside the cap
nothing changes. No existing verdict moved.

Refs #1303

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
